desc(
	mode: "source",
	language: "general",
	title: "Autoescape Disabled",
	title_zh: "检测到Autoescape Disabled",
	type: vuln,
	level: middle,
	rule_id: "source-insecure-api-autoescape-disabled",
	risk: "Security",
	desc: <<<DESC
Migrated from Semgrep rule `autoescape-disabled` (/tmp/semgrep-rules/java/lang/security/audit/xss/jsf/autoescape-disabled.yaml).
Original message: Detected an element with disabled HTML escaping. If external data can reach this, this is a cross-site scripting (XSS) vulnerability. Ensure no external data can reach here, or remove 'escape=false' from this element.

CWE: CWE-150: Improper Neutralization of Escape, Meta, or Control Sequences
References:
- https://stackoverflow.com/a/7442668

False-positive hardening: match only escape=false (not escape=true ... parse=false).
DESC,
	solution: <<<SOLUTION
Review the flagged code and follow the framework's secure coding guidance: use safe APIs, escape output, and avoid hardcoded credentials.
SOLUTION,
	alert_min: 1,
	"file://pos.html": <<<POS
<h:outputText value="#{user.input}" escape="false" />
POS,
	"safefile://neg.html": <<<NEG
<textarea escape="true"><#include "demo.html" parse=false/></textarea>
<h:outputText value="#{user.input}" escape="true" />
NEG,
)

${*.html}.pattern_regex(/(?i)\bescape\s*=\s*["']?false["']?/) as $p0
${*.xhtml}.pattern_regex(/(?i)\bescape\s*=\s*["']?false["']?/) as $p1
$p0 + $p1 as $hit
alert $hit for {
	level: "middle",
	title: "Autoescape Disabled",
	title_zh: "检测到Autoescape Disabled",
	message: "Autoescape Disabled",
}
